    language: {
        title: "HIDL Reference",
        page: [
            "# HIDL",
            "The interpreted language every .hor file is written in: layouts, data, strings and skins.",
            "",
            "## Values",
            "- Numbers `3`, `0.5`; strings `\"fight\"`; `true`, `false`, `null`",
            "- Vectors `vec(1, 2)`, `vec(0.2, 0.4, 0.9, 1)` for a colour",
            "- Objects `{ name: \"Ryu\", health: 100 }`, lists `[1, 2, 3]`",
            "",
            "## Code",
            "```hidl",
            "let speed = 3;",
            "const name = \"fight\";",
            "func add(a, b) { return a + b; }",
            "if (speed > 2) { print(\"fast\"); } else { print(\"slow\"); }",
            "for (item in [1, 2, 3]) { print(item); }",
            "let other = include(\"other.hor\");",
            "```",
            "",
            "## Directives",
            "A line starting with # is processed before the rest. `#define layout` marks the file as a layout, which Hex opens in the designer. Also `#define name value`, `#if defined(name)`, `#ifdef`, `#ifndef`, `#elif`, `#else`, `#endif`; code can query `defined(\"name\")` and `definition(\"name\")`.",
            "",
            "## Layouts",
            "```hidl",
            "#define layout",
            "let panel = compositor.stack({ spacing: 8 });",
            "let title = compositor.label({ parent: panel, text: \"@main_menu.title\" });",
            "let hud = compositor.include({ parent: panel, file: \"hud.hor\" });",
            "```",
            "A string starting with @ is a key of the game's strings. A label reads `[b]`, `[i]`, `[color:red]`, `$(save)` for an icon, and markdown when `markdown: true`. `compositor.include` builds another layout file inside a component; its parts are found by name as if written in the including file.",
            "",
            "## Strings files",
            "`let strings = { ... }`, a string per key, nested objects for dotted keys, and a list of strings for a multi-line text.",
            "",
            "## Library",
            "`print`, `include`, `keys`, `values`, `has`, `range`, `len`, `text`, `number`, `format`, `typeof`, `error`, `math` and `defined`. Hover any of them in the editor for details."
        ]
    },

    // What the pages of markdown say round the code they show
